=====Statistics=====
* According to the 2010 United States Census, ''China'' is the 29138<sup>th</sup> most common surname in the United States, belonging to 813 individuals. ''China'' is most common among Black/African-American (48.46%), White (17.47%), Hispanic (14.51%) and Asian/Pacific Islander (13.53%) individuals.

