===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=sound|:inh|enm:voys}}
{{dercat|en|itc-pro|ine-pro}}
From {{inh|en|enm|voice}}, {{m|enm|voys}}, {{m|enm|vois}}, borrowed from {{der|en|xno|[[voiz]], [[voys]], [[voice]]}}, {{der|en|fro|[[vois]], [[voiz]]}} (Modern {{cog|fr|voix}}), from {{der|en|la|vōcem}}, accusative form of {{m|la|vōx|t=voice}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sa|वाच्}}, {{cog|grc|ὄψ}}, {{cog|fa|آواز|tr=âvâz}}. Displaced native {{cog|enm|steven|t=voice}} (from {{cog|ang|stefn}} (see {{l|en|steven}})), {{cog|ang|hlēoþor#Noun}}, {{cog|ang|woþ#Noun_2}}, and {{cog|ang|reord#Noun}}. Compare {{m|en|advocate}}, {{m|en|advowson}}, {{m|en|avouch}}, {{m|en|convoke}}, {{m|en|vocal}}, {{m|en|vouch}}, {{m|en|vowel}}. {{doublet|en|vox}}.

