#* {{RQ:Milton Poems|poem=Nativity|page=2|passage=And joyn thy '''voice''' unto the Angel Quire,}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 10, 2011|author=Alistair Magowan| title=Aston Villa 1 - 0 Newcastle| work=BBC Sport| url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9446263.stm| passage=Villa chief executive Paul Faulkner had backed manager Houllier during the week and asked for the fans to get behind their team as they looked to steer themselves away from the relegation zone. <br>To that end, the home supporters were in good '''voice''' to begin with, but it was Newcastle who started the game in the ascendancy, with Barton putting a diving header over the top from Jose Enrique's cross.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260903052909/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9446263.stm|archivedate=3 September 2026}}
# {{lb|en|phonetics}} Sound made through vibration of the vocal cords; [[sonant]], or [[intonated]], utterance; tone; — distinguished from mere [[breath]] sound as heard in whispering and voiceless consonants.
# The [[tone]] or [[sound]] [[emitted]] by an [[object]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|1 Kings|19|12|text= And after the earthquake, a fire, but the Lord was not in the fire: and after the fire, a still small '''voice'''.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Job|40|9|text=Canst thou thunder with a '''voice''' like him?}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Psalms|93|3|text=The floods have lifted up their '''voice'''.}}
