#: {{ux|en|to cultivate the '''voice'''}}
# That which is [[communicated]]; [[message]]; [[meaning]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Galatians|4|20|text=I desire to bee present with you now, and to change my '''voyce''', for I stand in doubt of you.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|V|vii|passage=My '''voice''' is in my sword.}}
#* '''17th century''', {{w|John Fell (bishop)|John Fell}}, unknown work
#*: {{quote|en|Let us call on God in the '''voice''' of his church.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} An [[express]]ed [[opinion]], [[choice]], [[will]], [[desire]], or [[wish]]; the [[right]] or [[ability]] to [[make]] such [[expression]] or to [[have]] it [[consider]]ed.
#: {{syn|en|steven<q:obsolete>|vote|say-so}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Coriolanus|II|iii|passage=''Sicinius''. How now, my masters! have you chose this man? / ''1st Citizen''. He has our '''voices''', sir.}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aeneis|passage=Some laws ordain, and some attend the choice / Of holy senates, and elect by '''voice'''.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|url=https://edition.cnn.com/2019/03/22/asia/thai-election-young-voters-intl/index.html| author=Helen Regan; Kocha Olarn| date=2019-03-24| accessdate=2019-03-24| title=Thailand's youth demand change ahead of elections
|passage=Like many of the 7 million other first time voters, she came of age during half a decade of military rule that has governed the country since former general turned Prime Minister Prayut Chan-o-cha seized power in a 2014 coup. "We have had our '''voice''' taken away for five years," she says.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251009015225/https://edition.cnn.com/2019/03/22/asia/thai-election-young-voters-intl/index.html|archivedate=9 October 2025}}
